\name{cellucid_highlight_clear_all}
\alias{cellucid_highlight_clear_all}
\title{Clear every highlight}
\usage{
cellucid_highlight_clear_all(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Remove every group of every highlight page; the pages stay.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{highlight.clear-all} (Highlights). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{highlights}.
}
